00:59:45.663 --> 00:59:46.630
Just there.


00:59:46.664 --> 00:59:47.858
Is he in...?


00:59:47.899 --> 00:59:49.457
No, no, he's at school.


01:00:13.890 --> 01:00:16.154
Your son, is he studying
to be an architect?


01:00:16.192 --> 01:00:18.092
No, he's only 15.


01:00:18.127 --> 01:00:21.061
It's a school project.


01:00:25.067 --> 01:00:26.762
I'm an architect...


01:00:26.802 --> 01:00:28.565
of sorts.


01:00:28.603 --> 01:00:30.798
Hmm.


01:00:34.275 --> 01:00:35.242
(chuckles)


01:00:35.276 --> 01:00:37.073
Funny.


01:00:37.111 --> 01:00:40.080
Your son's project.


01:00:41.715 --> 01:00:42.682
We use those figures.


01:00:42.716 --> 01:00:43.705
They're scale figures.


01:00:43.751 --> 01:00:44.740
They're from Japan.


01:00:44.785 --> 01:00:46.411
Hard to find in London.


01:00:46.453 --> 01:00:47.715
Oh.


01:00:47.754 --> 01:00:49.381
He must get them from school.


01:00:52.425 --> 01:00:54.655
Uh, your trousers?


01:01:02.734 --> 01:01:04.395
You have, uh, children?


01:01:04.503 --> 01:01:06.562
Oh, you were with a little girl.


01:01:06.605 --> 01:01:08.300
- My daughter.
- Uh-huh.


01:01:08.340 --> 01:01:11.399
I remember her.


01:01:11.442 --> 01:01:14.605
This will take
a week, at least.


01:01:14.645 --> 01:01:15.873
I'll have to remove the lining.


01:01:15.913 --> 01:01:17.244
That's fine.


01:01:17.281 --> 01:01:19.977
I'll write you a bill
for the jacket.


01:01:25.589 --> 01:01:28.251
Should I just write "repairs"?


01:01:28.291 --> 01:01:29.622
Yeah.


01:01:35.198 --> 01:01:36.324
What's this?


01:01:37.666 --> 01:01:39.634
A practice keyboard.


01:01:39.668 --> 01:01:41.135
No space for piano up here.


01:01:41.170 --> 01:01:43.900
You can play electric
or electronic keyboard?


01:01:43.939 --> 01:01:47.033
Um, no, I'm happy with this.


01:01:47.076 --> 01:01:48.065
You know, I imagine.


01:01:48.110 --> 01:01:49.737
(hums melody)


01:01:49.778 --> 01:01:52.245
You know, so.


01:01:54.582 --> 01:01:57.016
Not a good place to make noises.


01:01:57.051 --> 01:01:59.952
You could always use headphones.


01:02:04.858 --> 01:02:07.793
I'm fixing this and I, um,
should mind my own business.


01:02:14.301 --> 01:02:18.396
People like me from my country,
we-- I'm Bosnian--


01:02:18.504 --> 01:02:21.871
we think it's dangerous
not to be able to hear.


01:02:38.623 --> 01:02:40.488
(door slides open)


01:02:42.860 --> 01:02:46.557
Tell your son
if he's interested,


01:02:46.597 --> 01:02:51.432
he can come and see our office,
you know, to look around.


01:02:51.502 --> 01:02:52.594
We're very close.


01:02:52.636 --> 01:02:53.864
King's Cross.


01:02:53.904 --> 01:02:56.133
I might do that.


01:02:58.074 --> 01:03:00.065
Will Francis is your name?


01:03:00.109 --> 01:03:01.736
- Mm.
- Hmm.


01:03:22.897 --> 01:03:24.990
(humming)


01:03:29.370 --> 01:03:31.463
(humming melody)


01:03:40.947 --> 01:03:44.110
(sniffling):
She'll never be his daughter.


01:03:44.150 --> 01:03:47.641
ROSEMARY: You wish Bea was
Will's daughter, is that it?


01:03:51.590 --> 01:03:52.989
I wish she was.


01:03:54.727 --> 01:03:56.194
I wish she was.


01:03:56.228 --> 01:03:59.890
Then maybe we'd all be happy.


01:04:02.967 --> 01:04:04.366
I don't want to be cold.


01:04:04.469 --> 01:04:06.232
I don't want to be sad.


01:04:06.271 --> 01:04:08.967
I don't want to be angry
with him anymore.


01:04:15.479 --> 01:04:16.969
I have this light box.


01:04:17.014 --> 01:04:18.208
What kind of light box?


01:04:18.248 --> 01:04:19.806
For depression.


01:04:19.850 --> 01:04:21.010
The doctor prescribed it


01:04:21.051 --> 01:04:23.076
and I sit in front of it
for hours.


01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:26.577
It's supposed to stop me
from getting down.


01:04:26.622 --> 01:04:32.686
Give me an image of that change
that you hope for in Will.


01:04:32.728 --> 01:04:35.322
He's looking at me.


01:04:38.099 --> 01:04:39.088
Sugar?


01:04:39.134 --> 01:04:40.533
Uh, no, thank you.


01:04:40.568 --> 01:04:44.504
I think you'll want sugar.


01:04:44.539 --> 01:04:45.836
Okay.


01:04:54.281 --> 01:04:55.748
Are you unhappy?


01:04:58.919 --> 01:05:00.409
What makes you say that?


01:05:00.454 --> 01:05:03.048
You always seem, when you
come here, I don't know.


01:05:06.459 --> 01:05:09.519
I'm happy enough.


01:05:09.562 --> 01:05:11.291
Happy enough.


01:05:11.331 --> 01:05:13.731
So English.


01:05:15.001 --> 01:05:16.195
(chuckles)


01:05:28.814 --> 01:05:32.715
LIV: I think it was
the happiest day, really...


01:05:32.750 --> 01:05:35.480
when Bea was born.


01:05:35.519 --> 01:05:39.546
And then sometimes I think...


01:05:39.590 --> 01:05:43.320
sometimes I think
Bea was punished


01:05:43.360 --> 01:05:47.387
because I left my husband
and I left Sweden.


01:05:47.430 --> 01:05:52.163
And then I met Will,
and he was kind.


01:05:55.904 --> 01:05:58.395
And we were happy,
we really were.


01:05:58.507 --> 01:06:03.308
But then I just push him away,
I don't know why.


01:06:03.345 --> 01:06:06.337
I just push him away from me.


01:06:09.484 --> 01:06:10.678
(doorbell ringing)


01:06:12.487 --> 01:06:15.945
Oh, this is, um, this is going
to sound really stupid.


01:06:15.990 --> 01:06:17.582
I forgot the shirt.


01:06:17.625 --> 01:06:20.321
I was going to bring a shirt


01:06:20.361 --> 01:06:22.555
for you, you to copy and...


01:06:22.596 --> 01:06:23.927
I forgot, I forgot it.


01:06:23.964 --> 01:06:25.864
Um, all right.


01:06:25.899 --> 01:06:27.491
Should I go back and get it?


01:06:27.534 --> 01:06:28.660
I can go back and get it now.


01:06:28.702 --> 01:06:30.863
And I'd be, like, two seconds.


01:06:30.904 --> 01:06:31.928
Okay.


01:06:31.972 --> 01:06:33.701
Or perhaps when you come
for the suit?


01:06:33.740 --> 01:06:35.764
It's a bad time?


01:06:35.808 --> 01:06:38.538
You mean without the shirt?


01:06:38.577 --> 01:06:41.876
Right, that doesn't make
any sense, does it?


01:06:41.914 --> 01:06:43.905
(chuckling)


01:06:43.949 --> 01:06:45.143
Uh...


01:06:45.184 --> 01:06:47.048
I'm going to the supermarket.


01:06:47.085 --> 01:06:48.552
- Right.
- I have to go to work.


01:06:48.586 --> 01:06:50.645
How do you get
the shopping home?


01:06:50.688 --> 01:06:52.121
Uh, bus.


01:06:52.157 --> 01:06:53.784
I'm practically driving a bus.


01:06:53.825 --> 01:06:56.487
My car's stolen,
so I have a company van.


01:06:56.528 --> 01:06:57.825
It's electric.


01:06:57.862 --> 01:06:58.886
You could probably walk faster.


01:06:58.930 --> 01:07:01.090
Pedestrians will overtake us.


01:07:01.131 --> 01:07:04.692
Say yes, and what's the worst
thing that could happen?


01:07:04.735 --> 01:07:05.997
Yes.


01:07:17.513 --> 01:07:19.504
Tell me about your son.


01:07:19.549 --> 01:07:22.040
- Mirsad?
- Mirsad?


01:07:22.084 --> 01:07:25.678
It's, um...


01:07:25.720 --> 01:07:26.880
He hates his name,


01:07:26.922 --> 01:07:31.188
but was a name for
Sarajevo, not for London.


01:07:31.226 --> 01:07:35.822
Now his name's Miro.


01:07:35.864 --> 01:07:38.128
But I think
he should love his name.


01:07:38.166 --> 01:07:39.598
You know, names in my country,


01:07:39.633 --> 01:07:41.760
they're like flags.


01:07:41.802 --> 01:07:46.171
You can live or die
because of your name.


01:07:46.207 --> 01:07:48.107
Mirsad-- it's a Muslim name.


01:07:48.142 --> 01:07:50.838
It should be Serbian
because of his father,


01:07:50.878 --> 01:07:53.937
but, you know,
I can be stubborn sometimes.


01:07:53.980 --> 01:07:54.947
You what?


01:07:54.981 --> 01:07:57.916
Stubborn sometimes.


01:07:57.951 --> 01:07:59.578
But that name saved his life.


01:07:59.619 --> 01:08:03.316
When we,
when we were getting out


01:08:03.389 --> 01:08:08.257
of Sarajevo, we came out with
Red Cross, leaving the siege.


01:08:08.293 --> 01:08:12.730
The guards, the Serbs, stopped
us at one of the checkpoints,


01:08:12.764 --> 01:08:15.028
and they took him,
they took my son,


01:08:15.067 --> 01:08:17.296
and they said what's your name?


01:08:17.335 --> 01:08:20.771
And he said, "Mirsad, my name
is Mirsad," his Muslim name.


01:08:20.805 --> 01:08:25.037
Well, if he told
his family name,


01:08:25.076 --> 01:08:26.703
the Serbian name, "Simic,"


01:08:26.744 --> 01:08:31.840
they might have taken him
as a son of a traitor.


01:08:31.882 --> 01:08:37.548
Anyway, since then, I don't
think he's ever really...


01:08:37.587 --> 01:08:39.987
He-he gets in trouble.


01:08:40.023 --> 01:08:41.718
That's another story.


01:08:41.758 --> 01:08:45.557
I can't talk about siege
in supermarket, sorry.


01:08:58.873 --> 01:09:02.434
We had a break-in.


01:09:02.477 --> 01:09:06.004
Several, actually,
in our office.


01:09:08.182 --> 01:09:09.307
Something gets smashed,


01:09:09.349 --> 01:09:12.284
I mean, I mean,
not just the windows.


01:09:16.456 --> 01:09:18.822
But not all breaking's bad,
is it, you know?


01:09:18.859 --> 01:09:21.123
I mean, you break habits.


01:09:21.161 --> 01:09:25.688
Maybe, maybe before
you repair the window,


01:09:25.731 --> 01:09:29.167
you should smash a few more.


01:09:29.201 --> 01:09:31.999
That's all I do, you see,
in my job, I tidy up.


01:09:32.038 --> 01:09:35.234
There's a mess between
buildings, and we come in.


01:09:35.273 --> 01:09:39.767
Squeeze in bits of green,
like dressing.


01:09:39.811 --> 01:09:41.540
Like lipstick,


01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:45.949
like pretty.


01:09:45.984 --> 01:09:52.582
Anyway, that's a roundabout way
of saying...


01:09:52.623 --> 01:09:54.113
the shape of your mouth,


01:09:54.158 --> 01:09:56.854
I could probably
draw it by heart.


01:10:03.766 --> 01:10:05.757
What are you thinking?


01:10:05.802 --> 01:10:10.136
I was thinking,
uh, that was a roundabout way


01:10:10.173 --> 01:10:12.141
of saying you're married,
which I know,


01:10:12.175 --> 01:10:14.768
and I was thinking


01:10:14.810 --> 01:10:17.904
Bosnian men would say less,
but, uh...


01:10:17.946 --> 01:10:21.177
would want more.


01:10:21.216 --> 01:10:24.652
They love to talk, they love
talk, believe me, but, uh,


01:10:24.686 --> 01:10:28.815
talk for them is politics,
women for them is not talk.


01:10:28.856 --> 01:10:31.586
That's crushing.


01:10:31.626 --> 01:10:33.526
(laughs)


01:10:33.561 --> 01:10:35.791
I didn't mean it bad.


01:10:44.638 --> 01:10:48.039
LIV: She's going to be
disappointed, but okay.


01:10:48.074 --> 01:10:51.737
MAN: Yeah. I have to take
the boys to cricket.


01:10:51.778 --> 01:10:54.712
(indistinct talking)


01:10:54.747 --> 01:10:56.009
Here's Mom.


01:10:56.048 --> 01:10:58.243
Dad can't make it.


01:10:58.283 --> 01:10:59.250
Aw...


01:10:59.284 --> 01:11:00.342
But here's what
we're going to do.


01:11:00.386 --> 01:11:01.250
It's okay.
Look, sweet...


01:11:01.286 --> 01:11:02.514
Why can't Dad come?


01:11:02.554 --> 01:11:04.351
Because he's working.
He can't make it in time.


01:11:04.423 --> 01:11:05.354
He never comes.


01:11:05.423 --> 01:11:06.822
We have the videos,
video, video, video.


01:11:06.858 --> 01:11:08.348
Hey! Hoopla.


01:11:08.459 --> 01:11:11.019
Stop. That stop there
is very good.


01:11:11.062 --> 01:11:12.552
I know. I realize.


01:11:14.232 --> 01:11:15.529
Again, again.


01:11:15.566 --> 01:11:17.193
- Again?
- Again.


01:11:17.235 --> 01:11:19.293
(cheering over TV)


01:11:19.336 --> 01:11:21.201
LIV (chuckling):
What do you think?


01:11:21.238 --> 01:11:22.705
- She's great, eh?
- Great.


01:11:22.739 --> 01:11:23.865
It's good, too,


01:11:23.907 --> 01:11:26.705
because the batteries
are back in the remote.


01:11:26.743 --> 01:11:29.211
It's a mystery how these
batteries finally went home


01:11:29.246 --> 01:11:31.372
just when we need them.


01:11:31.480 --> 01:11:34.210
Big mystery.


01:11:34.250 --> 01:11:37.708
Mystery two:
How did you video this


01:11:37.753 --> 01:11:39.345
and be in the picture
at the same time?


01:11:39.388 --> 01:11:40.514
Paul was cameraman.


01:11:40.556 --> 01:11:42.046
- Paul?
- Bea's trainer.


01:11:42.091 --> 01:11:43.388
You've met him a hundred times.


01:11:43.426 --> 01:11:44.722
Paul loves Mom.


01:11:44.759 --> 01:11:46.192
No, Paul loves Bea.


01:11:46.227 --> 01:11:47.956
(chuckles)


01:11:47.996 --> 01:11:50.692
But...


01:11:50.732 --> 01:11:52.996
does Paul love me?


01:11:56.337 --> 01:11:58.327
(inaudible chatter)


01:12:05.746 --> 01:12:09.477
(bell tolling in distance)


01:12:09.515 --> 01:12:15.078
WILL: If you could do anything
right now, what would it be?


01:12:15.121 --> 01:12:17.351
I have to work,
I have to get back.


01:12:17.457 --> 01:12:18.981
Oh, come on.


01:12:19.025 --> 01:12:21.255
(groans): Let me think.
I don't know, uh...


01:12:21.294 --> 01:12:22.851
(seagulls calling)


01:12:22.894 --> 01:12:25.863
Change everything up
until this moment.


01:12:25.897 --> 01:12:29.333
Uh, not my son, everything else.


01:12:29.367 --> 01:12:32.564
I can't do that for you.


01:12:32.604 --> 01:12:35.572
You didn't say
what could you do.


01:12:35.606 --> 01:12:37.471
What would I do is what you
said, not what you could do.


01:12:37.508 --> 01:12:39.567
What could I do?


01:12:42.646 --> 01:12:44.671
Why?


01:12:44.715 --> 01:12:47.013
I-I-I don't understand.


01:12:47.051 --> 01:12:50.281
I don't understand, either.


01:12:54.724 --> 01:12:58.251
If I had a magic
wand, I don't know,


01:12:58.294 --> 01:13:00.728
persuade my son to come
to Sarajevo with me,


01:13:00.764 --> 01:13:03.061
start a new life.


01:13:06.435 --> 01:13:10.201
And you, if you could
do anything right now,


01:13:10.239 --> 01:13:12.264
what would you do?


01:13:17.011 --> 01:13:18.911
I'm sorry. Sorry.


01:13:18.946 --> 01:13:20.607
I'm sorry.


01:13:45.971 --> 01:13:48.439
(children shouting in distance)


01:13:54.779 --> 01:13:56.110
(giggles)


01:14:00.251 --> 01:14:03.243
Hey, are you waking up?


01:14:03.288 --> 01:14:04.312
Mm-hmm.


01:14:04.355 --> 01:14:06.322
I made bread.


01:14:06.390 --> 01:14:07.789
I can smell them.


01:14:09.626 --> 01:14:11.617
It's hot. Careful.


01:14:18.335 --> 01:14:21.770
You're happy.


01:14:21.804 --> 01:14:24.500
Is that so strange?


01:14:24.540 --> 01:14:25.837
(chuckles)


01:14:25.875 --> 01:14:28.139
Put on the telly;
it might be on the news.


01:14:28.177 --> 01:14:31.907
Ha! You are not so big
I can sit on you.


01:14:31.947 --> 01:14:33.710
(laughs)


01:14:35.250 --> 01:14:36.877
Mm...


01:14:36.918 --> 01:14:39.284
Ah, Miro.


01:14:39.321 --> 01:14:42.222
Hmm...


01:14:42.257 --> 01:14:45.225
We should go home this
summer to Sarajevo.


01:14:45.259 --> 01:14:48.285
I think you would love it.


01:14:48.329 --> 01:14:51.628
Tanja says there are
flights for a few pounds.


01:14:51.665 --> 01:14:53.963
Maybe.


01:14:54.001 --> 01:14:57.095
Hmm.


01:14:57.137 --> 01:15:00.196
Maybe.


01:15:00.240 --> 01:15:03.004
Your grandmother
would cry for weeks.


01:15:03.042 --> 01:15:04.009
(both laugh)


01:15:04.043 --> 01:15:05.010
Great.


01:15:11.583 --> 01:15:12.914
(door closes)


01:15:25.763 --> 01:15:27.094
(camera beeps)


01:15:44.981 --> 01:15:47.279
What's this?


01:15:47.317 --> 01:15:50.012
Oh, uh, I-I forgot.


01:15:50.052 --> 01:15:51.781
- I put it in your room.
- Where'd you get it?


01:15:51.820 --> 01:15:53.014
It's a customer.


01:15:53.055 --> 01:15:54.022
I sewed his jacket.


01:15:54.056 --> 01:15:55.250
He's an architect.


01:15:55.291 --> 01:15:57.088
He said, uh, you could go
and look at his office.


01:15:57.126 --> 01:15:58.787
What's the matter?


01:15:58.827 --> 01:15:59.794
I have to go out.


01:15:59.828 --> 01:16:00.795
What did you say to him?


01:16:00.829 --> 01:16:03.422
Wh-Wh-What do you mean?


01:16:03.464 --> 01:16:04.522
Did he go in my room?!


01:16:04.565 --> 01:16:06.624
No. Just to try some trousers.


01:16:06.668 --> 01:16:08.431
Why do people have
to go into my room?!


01:16:08.469 --> 01:16:10.494
Miro, <i>dushma</i>, he's a good
person, he's a good man.


01:16:10.538 --> 01:16:11.766
He was just trying to help.


01:16:11.806 --> 01:16:13.273
You think everyone is good.


01:16:13.308 --> 01:16:14.639
No one is good.


01:16:20.447 --> 01:16:21.914
What are you...


01:16:21.949 --> 01:16:23.644
(clattering)


01:16:23.684 --> 01:16:25.311
What is it?


01:16:25.419 --> 01:16:28.251
I'm in such shit.


01:16:36.662 --> 01:16:38.960
MIRO:
She's taken back the laptop.


01:16:38.998 --> 01:16:40.295
ZORAN:
She what?


01:16:40.333 --> 01:16:42.493
She's taken back the laptop.


01:16:42.534 --> 01:16:46.026
That is so fucked up.


01:16:47.038 --> 01:16:48.335
She says they're friends.


01:16:48.440 --> 01:16:50.908
Yeah, but that's like,
"Hello, my son did it.


01:16:50.942 --> 01:16:52.842
Lock him up."


01:16:52.877 --> 01:16:57.176
She says she's going to talk
to him, do some sort of deal.


01:16:57.214 --> 01:17:01.651
Papa.
Papa.


01:17:08.725 --> 01:17:09.714
WOMAN:
Will!


01:17:09.759 --> 01:17:10.783
WILL:
What?


01:17:10.827 --> 01:17:13.091
Lady looking for you.


01:17:13.129 --> 01:17:14.596
What?


01:17:14.630 --> 01:17:17.724
A lady is looking for you.


01:17:34.849 --> 01:17:36.146
Are you okay?


01:17:36.183 --> 01:17:37.616
What is it you want from me?


01:17:37.651 --> 01:17:38.982
Nothing, I don't want anything.


01:17:39.020 --> 01:17:40.988
Because you don't just walk
into someone's life


01:17:41.022 --> 01:17:42.990
and knock on their door
and kiss them.


01:17:43.024 --> 01:17:44.321
- You cannot do that.
- I know that.


01:17:44.358 --> 01:17:45.984
What? What-what's the matter?


01:17:46.026 --> 01:17:47.323
You used me;
you have someone else.


01:17:47.427 --> 01:17:48.917
- Oh, you mean Liv?
- Promise me, promise me.


01:17:48.962 --> 01:17:50.088
That's the last thing I want,
believe...


01:17:50.130 --> 01:17:51.427
Promise you what?


01:17:51.464 --> 01:17:52.829
Promise you I'm not flirting?


01:17:52.866 --> 01:17:54.333
- I know what that is.
- I don't believe you.


01:17:54.367 --> 01:17:55.629
I know what that is,


01:17:55.668 --> 01:17:57.135
- and this is not what it is.
- I don't believe you.


01:17:57.170 --> 01:17:58.659
I don't...


01:18:01.173 --> 01:18:03.073
I can't talk anymore.


01:18:03.108 --> 01:18:05.872
I want to go somewhere
and not talk.


01:18:05.911 --> 01:18:08.402
Not talk.


01:18:10.416 --> 01:18:13.282
I have a friend;
she... she works.


01:18:13.317 --> 01:18:16.616
Maybe she would lend her place.


01:18:16.654 --> 01:18:17.882
It's close to here.


01:18:17.922 --> 01:18:19.287
Call her.


01:18:19.323 --> 01:18:20.620
It's not a hotel,
it's not a palace


01:18:20.658 --> 01:18:21.647
Call her.


01:18:23.661 --> 01:18:26.561
What's her number?


01:18:43.779 --> 01:18:46.680
(inaudible chatter,
keys jingling)


01:19:15.476 --> 01:19:18.706
##


01:19:58.448 --> 01:20:03.750
The clothes under my
clothes, they're not...


01:20:03.786 --> 01:20:07.812
I've always wanted to
make something in silk.


01:20:13.996 --> 01:20:17.591
I'm, uh, giving myself to you.


01:20:17.633 --> 01:20:21.295
I want it to be worth something.


01:20:23.004 --> 01:20:25.768
Come here.


01:20:55.768 --> 01:20:58.895
##


01:21:27.630 --> 01:21:29.359
(mouthing words)


01:21:44.446 --> 01:21:48.075
##


01:22:04.864 --> 01:22:09.961
(siren wailing in distance)


01:22:15.575 --> 01:22:18.441
- WILL: Hi.
- Hi.


01:22:18.477 --> 01:22:23.312
I'm, uh, I never met somebody
when I was already in their bed.


01:22:23.415 --> 01:22:24.848
I'm Will.


01:22:24.883 --> 01:22:26.942
Thank you.


01:22:26.985 --> 01:22:28.509
I'm Tanja.


01:22:28.553 --> 01:22:30.816
It's good to have
a man in my bed.


01:22:30.855 --> 01:22:33.824
I hope it's contagious.


01:22:35.159 --> 01:22:38.492
I'll get my, uh...


01:23:01.717 --> 01:23:05.448
BEA: "'Don't kill the boy,'
Brave Benoit said,


01:23:05.487 --> 01:23:07.284
"but Dai replied,


01:23:07.389 --> 01:23:11.290
"'Why not? I come
from the Isle of Wight.


01:23:11.326 --> 01:23:13.487
"We eat young boys a lot.'


01:23:13.528 --> 01:23:17.020
"But secretly, Dai had a heart.


01:23:17.065 --> 01:23:19.533
"He kept it in a jar.


01:23:19.567 --> 01:23:21.932
"He hadn't seen
that jar for years.


01:23:21.968 --> 01:23:24.300
He found it in his car."


01:23:24.404 --> 01:23:25.803
Great reading.


01:23:25.839 --> 01:23:28.501
That's not reading,
that's knowing by heart.


01:23:28.542 --> 01:23:30.009
There's a metaphor.


01:23:30.043 --> 01:23:31.408
Where?


01:23:31.445 --> 01:23:34.208
WILL:
To know by heart.


01:23:34.246 --> 01:23:41.084
"'Forgive, forget, and eat more
jam,' the jar said on the lid.


01:23:41.120 --> 01:23:44.817
"Dai ate some jam
and thought a lot,


01:23:44.857 --> 01:23:47.586
"and in the end, he did.


01:23:47.625 --> 01:23:51.618
ALL:
"Go home and be a better boy,


01:23:51.663 --> 01:23:54.791
"although sometimes,
it's tricky.


01:23:54.833 --> 01:23:58.325
"There is a moral to this tale:


01:23:58.370 --> 01:24:02.806
Jam makes fingers sticky."


01:24:02.840 --> 01:24:04.137
(giggles)


01:24:04.174 --> 01:24:05.141
Well done.


01:24:05.175 --> 01:24:07.507
Sticky jam.


01:24:07.544 --> 01:24:10.240
Okay, my sweetie.


01:24:10.280 --> 01:24:13.680
It is now time
for you and bunny


01:24:13.716 --> 01:24:16.651
(squeaky-voiced):
to get some sleep.


01:24:16.686 --> 01:24:20.281
(distant chatter)


01:24:20.390 --> 01:24:22.585
(speaking Bosnian)


01:24:27.629 --> 01:24:29.722
You're a monkey,
be a wise monkey.


01:24:29.765 --> 01:24:33.223
Somebody asks you a question,
you know nothing,


01:24:33.268 --> 01:24:34.735
you see nothing,


01:24:34.770 --> 01:24:36.897
you hear nothing.


01:24:37.005 --> 01:24:38.631
I'm not a monkey for sure.


01:24:39.006 --> 01:24:42.032
Your mother's a Muslim dog.
They have loose tongues.


01:24:42.076 --> 01:24:44.738
Are you my brother's son,
or your mother's?


01:24:44.779 --> 01:24:45.973
We'll find out.


01:24:47.481 --> 01:24:48.846
And you don't come
to the car wash.


01:24:48.883 --> 01:24:51.248
You don't come to our house...


01:24:51.284 --> 01:24:55.311
If the police find anything,
we're all going to prison...


01:24:55.355 --> 01:24:56.686
Hurry up!


01:25:11.703 --> 01:25:13.864
You're a thief-- I'll kill you!


01:25:15.441 --> 01:25:16.499
Go ahead, dent the dents.


01:25:16.542 --> 01:25:18.873
Get away from my boy!


01:25:18.910 --> 01:25:22.437
It's no wonder my brother
was fucking someone else.


01:25:22.580 --> 01:25:25.014
(shouting)


01:25:28.486 --> 01:25:30.112
I don't want you
in this house!


01:25:30.153 --> 01:25:32.553
- Sure, whatever.
- Understand?


01:25:32.589 --> 01:25:34.386
(door slams)


01:25:37.461 --> 01:25:39.725
Mirsad.


01:25:44.733 --> 01:25:46.792
Why didn't you give it back?


01:25:46.836 --> 01:25:49.396
I will, I will.


01:25:49.438 --> 01:25:51.269
I will give it back.


01:25:51.307 --> 01:25:52.899
I don't get it.


01:25:52.942 --> 01:25:54.637
He knows, doesn't he?


01:25:54.677 --> 01:25:57.042
Why doesn't he just
tell the police?


01:25:58.746 --> 01:26:00.338
I don't get it.


01:26:13.727 --> 01:26:16.719
##


01:26:30.042 --> 01:26:31.600
Will?


01:26:31.644 --> 01:26:33.635
Yeah.


01:26:35.347 --> 01:26:36.644
You should come and see this.


01:26:36.681 --> 01:26:38.205
- What?
- Come... come see.


01:26:46.825 --> 01:26:49.190
Just left here.


01:26:49.226 --> 01:26:50.625
Keys are inside.


01:27:01.571 --> 01:27:03.334
(engine starts,
rock music blaring)


01:27:03.373 --> 01:27:07.901
# I need... a man #


01:27:09.879 --> 01:27:11.904
(music stops, Will chuckles)


01:27:17.352 --> 01:27:18.944
What does that mean?


01:27:18.987 --> 01:27:21.854
I don't know.


01:27:21.890 --> 01:27:24.484
Will, is there something
going on with you?


01:27:24.526 --> 01:27:26.459
(sighs)


01:27:26.494 --> 01:27:28.894
I don't know.


01:27:31.165 --> 01:27:32.462
(clears throat)


01:27:32.500 --> 01:27:34.263
Something's going on with me.


01:27:34.302 --> 01:27:36.964
Erika, you know, Erika...


01:27:37.004 --> 01:27:41.030
(clears throat)
...forgave me, and, uh, well...


01:27:41.074 --> 01:27:44.009
(chuckles)
It's early doors, but you know,


01:27:44.044 --> 01:27:48.208
you know,
lattes have been drunk.


01:27:49.449 --> 01:27:51.542
- That's great.
- (chuckles)


01:27:51.585 --> 01:27:54.178
Sandy, can we go somewhere?
Can we drive somewhere now?


01:27:54.219 --> 01:27:55.811
- Will...
- Anywhere?


01:27:55.854 --> 01:27:57.651
(clears throat): Don't tell me
you're fooling around, okay?


01:27:57.690 --> 01:27:59.658
I'm just entering fidelity;
don't exit.


01:27:59.692 --> 01:28:01.250
It's not about fooling around.


01:28:01.293 --> 01:28:03.193
It's always
about fooling around.


01:28:07.098 --> 01:28:08.622
- (screeching)
- Fucking hell.


01:28:08.666 --> 01:28:11.226
(chuckles)


01:28:11.302 --> 01:28:14.829
(yelping)


01:28:14.872 --> 01:28:16.203
(chuckles)


01:28:19.309 --> 01:28:22.073
Will, I've, I've got to...


01:28:22.112 --> 01:28:23.977
and so have you.


01:28:30.820 --> 01:28:33.721
(up-tempo hip-hop song playing)


01:28:41.430 --> 01:28:43.398
BRUNO:
Oi!


01:28:43.432 --> 01:28:45.262
Where do you
think you're going?


01:28:45.333 --> 01:28:46.664
Get on the back.


01:28:46.701 --> 01:28:47.929
I'm late for school.


01:28:47.969 --> 01:28:50.995
Yeah, two years late--
get on the back.


01:28:51.039 --> 01:28:54.065
You're in a lot of trouble, son.


01:28:55.443 --> 01:28:58.707
Put your helmet on;
it makes you invisible.


01:28:58.746 --> 01:29:01.010
(engine starts)


01:29:01.048 --> 01:29:03.312
And don't stab me
while I'm driving.


01:29:03.350 --> 01:29:06.114
You'll fall off.


01:29:10.890 --> 01:29:12.221
Everybody's chasing around
looking for evidence--


01:29:12.291 --> 01:29:13.849
fingerprints, DNA.


01:29:13.893 --> 01:29:15.224
I just look at the buildings


01:29:15.294 --> 01:29:17.728
and I know it's you.
I know.


01:29:17.764 --> 01:29:20.528
Someone's doing very well,
and you're not.


01:29:20.566 --> 01:29:23.932
I mean, what do you earn,
a few quid, pair of trainers?


01:29:23.969 --> 01:29:26.597
You're the bit
you spit out to your friends--


01:29:26.638 --> 01:29:28.799
whoever they are--
and I know who they are.


01:29:28.840 --> 01:29:30.671
They're not your friends.


01:29:30.709 --> 01:29:31.903
How long are we staying?


01:29:31.943 --> 01:29:35.343
Ah... she's lovely.


01:29:36.914 --> 01:29:38.347
(sighs)


01:29:38.382 --> 01:29:41.044
They should tip London on its
side and let a few million


01:29:41.085 --> 01:29:42.518
people slide right off, you see?


01:29:42.553 --> 01:29:43.679
There's no air.


01:29:45.723 --> 01:29:48.748
There's no air in a cell.


01:29:48.792 --> 01:29:50.623
None.


01:29:50.660 --> 01:29:54.255
And that's where
you're going, no question,


01:29:54.330 --> 01:29:57.390
and that's a tragedy.


01:30:08.610 --> 01:30:11.602
Which of us is lying the most?


01:30:11.647 --> 01:30:14.114
About what?


01:30:14.148 --> 01:30:17.549
That's not even
the right question.


01:30:17.585 --> 01:30:20.611
Which of us is lying
to themselves the most?


01:30:20.655 --> 01:30:22.282
What?


01:30:22.390 --> 01:30:25.655
About this.


01:30:25.693 --> 01:30:28.092
I'm not lying.


01:30:31.431 --> 01:30:34.025
I have, um...


01:30:34.067 --> 01:30:36.092
a photograph.


01:30:36.136 --> 01:30:37.933
What photograph?


01:30:37.971 --> 01:30:39.870
Of us.


01:30:39.905 --> 01:30:41.634
It's, uh...


01:30:41.674 --> 01:30:44.939
incriminating is-is
the right the word.


01:30:44.977 --> 01:30:47.309
I don't know
if it's the right word,


01:30:47.379 --> 01:30:50.007
unless I know
what you're talking about.


01:30:50.049 --> 01:30:52.449
It took me a...


01:30:52.485 --> 01:30:56.011
a little while to make
sense of the jacket.


01:30:56.054 --> 01:30:59.820
You suddenly
appearing at my door.


01:30:59.858 --> 01:31:02.725
That you'd been
following my son.


01:31:02.761 --> 01:31:04.058
(sighs)


01:31:04.095 --> 01:31:05.823
You must know that mothers


01:31:05.863 --> 01:31:09.959
will do anything to protect
their children.


01:31:10.000 --> 01:31:12.764
Why-Why would you
take a photograph?


01:31:12.803 --> 01:31:15.533
Was that when your
friend came back?


01:31:17.241 --> 01:31:18.901
Why would you do that?


01:31:18.941 --> 01:31:22.638
Why would you do this?


01:31:22.678 --> 01:31:25.977
You steal someone's heart;
that's a real crime.


01:31:26.015 --> 01:31:28.745
And then what?
You call the police?


01:31:28.785 --> 01:31:30.275
No.


01:31:30.386 --> 01:31:32.649
I don't know... No!


01:31:32.687 --> 01:31:37.215
Did you know how long...


01:31:37.259 --> 01:31:38.851
(sighs)


01:31:40.762 --> 01:31:43.663
Do you know how long
since anybody touched me?


01:31:45.499 --> 01:31:48.468
I should have told you, I know.
I should have said something.


01:31:48.502 --> 01:31:50.766
It wasn't a plan.


01:31:50.805 --> 01:31:53.569
It wasn't a plan--
it was you, that's the truth.


01:31:55.309 --> 01:31:56.936
I have to get out.


01:31:56.977 --> 01:31:58.876
Is that why you come
to bed with me?


01:31:58.912 --> 01:32:00.641
For what, a photograph?


01:32:00.680 --> 01:32:02.910
How squalid.


01:32:05.151 --> 01:32:08.018
The water is cold.


01:32:08.054 --> 01:32:09.749
But what about...?
But it...


01:32:09.789 --> 01:32:10.880
It doesn't make any sense.


01:32:10.923 --> 01:32:12.015
What about today?


01:32:12.057 --> 01:32:14.082
Or now?


01:32:14.126 --> 01:32:16.026
Look, a lie, that's
right. That's my...


01:32:16.061 --> 01:32:18.029
That's me--
I lie, I lie.


01:32:18.063 --> 01:32:20.623
Can't we drawn a line and
say no more lies between us?


01:32:20.666 --> 01:32:22.190
No more lies.


01:32:22.234 --> 01:32:24.929
No, I have to ask you to lie,
to continue to lie.


01:32:24.969 --> 01:32:28.598
I have to beg you
not to report my son.


01:32:28.639 --> 01:32:33.099
That's what this is: a bribe.


01:32:33.144 --> 01:32:36.044
If you like.


01:32:43.854 --> 01:32:46.084
I'm, um... not stopping.


01:32:46.122 --> 01:32:49.579
Old Bill's been at our place.


01:32:49.625 --> 01:32:53.220
He says he's going to
try and charge my dad.


01:32:53.262 --> 01:32:54.854
You shouldn't be here.


01:32:54.897 --> 01:32:57.127
What if they followed you?
Then what?


01:32:57.166 --> 01:33:01.227
So? There's nothing for them
to find here, is there?


01:33:01.270 --> 01:33:02.600
They've been down
the car wash, as well,


01:33:02.637 --> 01:33:03.604
making out with
all this evidence.


01:33:03.638 --> 01:33:06.038
They've got nothing.
Trust me, nothing.


01:33:06.074 --> 01:33:08.736
(hip-hop music playing
in distance)


01:33:11.112 --> 01:33:12.238
Hey!


01:33:12.347 --> 01:33:14.406
Zoran! The laptop!


01:33:14.449 --> 01:33:16.507
They'll find my laptop!


01:33:17.784 --> 01:33:19.684
OFFICER:
Oi!


01:33:19.720 --> 01:33:21.483
(panting)


01:33:21.521 --> 01:33:23.489
Up there!


01:33:23.523 --> 01:33:24.751
Come on!


01:33:28.027 --> 01:33:29.392
(both panting)


01:33:29.428 --> 01:33:31.658
Get to the other end.


01:33:31.697 --> 01:33:33.688
- Come on!
- Come on!


01:33:39.505 --> 01:33:40.437
Don't do it!


01:33:40.473 --> 01:33:42.099
Hey!


01:33:45.610 --> 01:33:47.009
Little bastards are going


01:33:47.045 --> 01:33:49.343
through Eastern Avenue,
Eastern Avenue, on their way!


01:33:54.451 --> 01:33:57.352
(sirens wailing)


01:34:03.327 --> 01:34:05.955
OFFICER:
The towpath!


01:34:06.663 --> 01:34:08.221
(groans)


01:34:08.298 --> 01:34:09.458
Miro!


01:34:09.499 --> 01:34:11.626
- Miro!
- OFFICER: I'll head him off.


01:34:11.668 --> 01:34:14.728
Miro!
Miro!


01:34:14.771 --> 01:34:16.136
(groans)


01:34:16.172 --> 01:34:19.141
Don't, don't move him.


01:34:19.175 --> 01:34:20.106
Come on!


01:34:20.142 --> 01:34:22.667
Don't move!


01:34:27.749 --> 01:34:31.947
(chorus singing in Bosnian)


01:34:45.465 --> 01:34:48.866
(song continues)


01:35:04.683 --> 01:35:06.844
(indistinct whispering)


01:35:14.325 --> 01:35:17.488
##


01:35:23.034 --> 01:35:24.295
(singing fades)


01:35:39.281 --> 01:35:40.748
(door clangs)


01:35:45.221 --> 01:35:47.052
I'm sorry.


01:35:56.898 --> 01:35:58.729
WILL:
You going to be okay?


01:35:58.767 --> 01:35:59.893
Uh-huh.


01:35:59.934 --> 01:36:01.697
Show Mommy she can go
to her work,


01:36:01.736 --> 01:36:03.669
we can do ours.


01:36:03.704 --> 01:36:06.138
Hmm?


01:36:06.173 --> 01:36:08.539
Wei Ping, can you just...?


01:36:08.575 --> 01:36:09.974
MAN: ...exactly as it says
on the model.


01:36:10.010 --> 01:36:11.341
Number nine needs to go left.


01:36:11.378 --> 01:36:12.538
All right, take it back, please.


01:36:12.579 --> 01:36:13.546
Yeah, way left.


01:36:13.580 --> 01:36:15.479
To the very end.


01:36:15.515 --> 01:36:18.313
At least three feet to the left.


01:36:18.351 --> 01:36:19.409
The model's not bad.


01:36:19.452 --> 01:36:20.476
Number nine is.


01:36:20.520 --> 01:36:21.418
Way back!


01:36:21.454 --> 01:36:22.443
- Will?
- Yeah?


01:36:22.488 --> 01:36:23.455
A couple colleagues of mine.


01:36:23.489 --> 01:36:25.047
This is Erin and Lorna,
this is Mr. Francis.


01:36:25.091 --> 01:36:26.058
- Hello.
- Hello.


01:36:26.092 --> 01:36:27.992
Was a fair result all
around on the burglary,


01:36:28.027 --> 01:36:31.325
and the DNA matched, and we got
most of your stolen goods back.


01:36:31.363 --> 01:36:34.491
Yes, Sandy said, um,
he's a young boy?


01:36:34.533 --> 01:36:35.625
Yeah, he's 15.


01:36:35.667 --> 01:36:36.827
He's been in and out of trouble.


01:36:36.868 --> 01:36:38.563
You know, final warning.


01:36:38.603 --> 01:36:39.763
He's going to prison.


01:36:39.805 --> 01:36:41.772
BRUNO: If he gets
convicted he will, yes.


01:36:41.806 --> 01:36:43.501
He'll go to Youth
Detention Center.


01:36:43.541 --> 01:36:45.099
Is this your computer, Will?


01:36:45.142 --> 01:36:46.507
It's got all your files on it.


01:36:46.544 --> 01:36:48.068
Well, then it must be.
Great.


01:36:48.112 --> 01:36:50.171
ERIN: Well, I'm afraid
we're going to have to keep it


01:36:50.214 --> 01:36:51.545
just until the case
comes to court.


01:36:51.582 --> 01:36:53.880
Bea? Bea, no!


01:36:53.918 --> 01:36:55.111
- Bea!
- Wei Ping, could you just...?


01:36:55.151 --> 01:36:56.175
I'm okay, I'm fine.


01:36:56.219 --> 01:36:57.948
Darling, stay with Wei Ping.


01:36:57.987 --> 01:36:59.454
This is a hollow victory for us,
ain't it, girls?


01:36:59.489 --> 01:37:00.478
It is, yeah.


01:37:00.523 --> 01:37:01.922
I mean, he's just
the little runt


01:37:01.958 --> 01:37:03.186
who's done all the dirty work.


01:37:03.226 --> 01:37:05.558
We can't make a case
against the adults.


01:37:05.595 --> 01:37:07.289
They're the real villains.


01:37:07.329 --> 01:37:08.318
Yeah, it's hollow.


01:37:08.363 --> 01:37:09.660
Well, you may find it hollow,


01:37:09.698 --> 01:37:11.598
we find it whatever
is the opposite of hollow.


01:37:11.633 --> 01:37:12.793
Of course, we understand.


01:37:12.835 --> 01:37:14.302
Because actually, it's been
like a siege, okay?


01:37:14.336 --> 01:37:16.930
We have felt under siege,
and worse than that,


01:37:16.972 --> 01:37:18.940
innocent people have been
wrongly accused, our cleaners,


01:37:18.974 --> 01:37:20.201
you know, it's very degrading.


01:37:20.241 --> 01:37:21.538
It's because we know the boy,
you know?


01:37:21.576 --> 01:37:23.009
I mean, there's nothing wrong
with him.


01:37:23.044 --> 01:37:25.205
Nothing wrong? He's a thief,
that's what's wrong with him.


01:37:25.246 --> 01:37:26.213
Well, there's no question.


01:37:26.247 --> 01:37:30.206
Will, all this
is about some court...


01:37:30.318 --> 01:37:33.115
- It's not a court.
- Conciliation court.


01:37:33.153 --> 01:37:35.678
Whereby, if we go along
to meet the boy...


01:37:35.722 --> 01:37:36.586
What is it?


01:37:36.623 --> 01:37:38.113
Explain, it's a Camden thing.


01:37:38.158 --> 01:37:39.591
He gets let off, hooray.


01:37:39.626 --> 01:37:40.923
It's not a court.


01:37:40.961 --> 01:37:42.895
Me and Lorna, we work
on the Youth Offenders team,


01:37:42.929 --> 01:37:45.557
and we encourage the offenders
to face their victims.


01:37:45.599 --> 01:37:47.828
Right, so we go to the court,
arrange to meet him...


01:37:47.867 --> 01:37:49.528
Not a court, sorry,
whatever court it is,


01:37:49.568 --> 01:37:51.001
and he might not go to prison?


01:37:51.036 --> 01:37:52.003
Yeah, that's right, yeah.


01:37:52.037 --> 01:37:54.471
The law's an ass.


01:37:54.507 --> 01:37:56.236
BRUNO:
Look, he's a boy.


01:37:56.308 --> 01:37:57.866
The last thing he needs
is prison.


01:37:57.910 --> 01:38:01.640
ERIN: You know he's a Bosnian
boy, and his mom, well,


01:38:01.679 --> 01:38:03.044
well, they're refugees,


01:38:03.081 --> 01:38:05.015
and his mom's,
his mom's in pieces.


01:38:05.049 --> 01:38:06.949
BRUNO: Mr. Francis,
what do you think?


01:38:06.985 --> 01:38:08.384
You've been very quiet.


01:38:08.419 --> 01:38:11.582
I just, I want to draw a line
under the whole thing.


01:38:11.623 --> 01:38:12.816
(screams)


01:38:12.856 --> 01:38:14.824
Bea!


01:38:21.231 --> 01:38:23.529
WOMAN:
Somebody call an ambulance!


01:38:23.567 --> 01:38:25.534
WEI PING:
I'm so sorry! I am so sorry!


01:38:25.568 --> 01:38:26.592
All right, don't move.


01:38:26.636 --> 01:38:27.933
It's gonna be all right.


01:38:27.970 --> 01:38:29.631
I'm here, I'm here.


01:38:34.477 --> 01:38:35.808
(sobbing):
I'm so sorry.


01:38:46.354 --> 01:38:47.412
Hi, sweetie.


01:38:47.455 --> 01:38:48.888
My fibula's broken, two places.


01:38:48.924 --> 01:38:50.186
Ouch.


01:38:50.225 --> 01:38:52.886
And they have to put wires in
to fix it.


01:38:52.927 --> 01:38:53.894
Oh.


01:38:53.928 --> 01:38:56.158
The doctor said, she said what?


01:38:56.197 --> 01:38:59.064
She said that I'd be up
and climbing again in no time.


01:38:59.099 --> 01:39:01.363
Hmm. We've got an X-ray
if you want to see.


01:39:01.402 --> 01:39:02.300
Definitely.


01:39:02.336 --> 01:39:04.360
BEA:
Sorry.


01:39:04.404 --> 01:39:05.666
Oh, sweetie, don't be sorry.


01:39:05.705 --> 01:39:06.763
<i>I'm</i> sorry.


01:39:06.806 --> 01:39:08.364
I'm sorriest.


01:39:08.408 --> 01:39:10.842
- Daddy cried.
- I did not.


01:39:10.877 --> 01:39:12.469
I laughed on the wrong
side of my face.


01:39:12.512 --> 01:39:14.571
- Is it hurting?
- It did.


01:39:16.248 --> 01:39:17.738
We had painkillers.


01:39:17.783 --> 01:39:19.148
Bea had two, daddy had four.


01:39:19.184 --> 01:39:20.674
You did not.


01:39:20.719 --> 01:39:24.177
So, listen, Mommy's going
to stay, okay?


01:39:24.289 --> 01:39:25.313
And I brought everything.


01:39:25.357 --> 01:39:27.985
I brought Stuffy.


01:39:28.026 --> 01:39:29.788
This hospital's very peculiar.


01:39:29.827 --> 01:39:31.021
They don't understand
color, do they?


01:39:31.062 --> 01:39:33.030
Tried to put us
in a yellow room.


01:39:33.064 --> 01:39:34.395
I need to speak to Mommy.


01:39:34.432 --> 01:39:36.593
Mommy's here.


01:39:36.634 --> 01:39:38.192
I need to speak
to Mommy by myself.


01:39:38.302 --> 01:39:40.395
Will?


01:39:40.438 --> 01:39:42.428
Okay.


01:39:46.910 --> 01:39:50.812
(computerized voice on phone):
You have four new messages.


01:39:50.847 --> 01:39:52.747
Hello, Will, it's Amira.


01:39:52.782 --> 01:39:53.942
I need to see you.


01:39:53.984 --> 01:39:56.042
Uh, call me. Thank you.


01:39:56.085 --> 01:39:59.384
Hello, Will, it's Amira. Uh...


01:40:05.761 --> 01:40:06.921
I'm sorry.


01:40:08.930 --> 01:40:13.196
First of all, I want
to give you this,


01:40:13.234 --> 01:40:16.362
which are the pictures.


01:40:19.540 --> 01:40:21.234
I wish, I wish
they hadn't caught him.


01:40:21.275 --> 01:40:25.041
I wish I hadn't hurt you.


01:40:25.078 --> 01:40:26.909
Truly.


01:40:26.947 --> 01:40:28.209
Then help me. Help him.


01:40:28.248 --> 01:40:31.240
I can't.


01:40:31.351 --> 01:40:34.183
This meeting with Miro and
police, if you came, it would...


01:40:34.220 --> 01:40:36.347
I really can't.


01:40:36.389 --> 01:40:38.789
He'll go to prison.


01:40:40.660 --> 01:40:42.059
He's agreed, Miro.


01:40:42.094 --> 01:40:44.927
If you help him, he'll come
back with me to Sarajevo.


01:40:44.964 --> 01:40:47.056
He won't say anything in court
except he's sorry,


01:40:47.098 --> 01:40:48.360
I promise you.


01:40:48.400 --> 01:40:51.267
You're a good person;
I know you.


01:40:51.369 --> 01:40:53.769
- Don't do that. Don't do that.
- Please.


01:40:53.805 --> 01:40:55.067
- Don't do that.
- Please.


01:40:55.106 --> 01:40:57.006
Amira, I can't,
I can't do what you want.


01:40:57.042 --> 01:40:58.270
How can I?


01:40:58.310 --> 01:41:01.142
If I meet your son, it will come
out that I know you,


01:41:01.178 --> 01:41:02.668
how I know you.


01:41:02.713 --> 01:41:03.737
Please, help me.


01:41:03.781 --> 01:41:06.409
I can't help you.
I can't help you.


01:41:06.450 --> 01:41:07.849
I can't.
I'm sorry.


01:41:07.885 --> 01:41:09.546
Please! Please!


01:41:09.586 --> 01:41:12.554
Listen, I really tried
to get him out of trouble.


01:41:12.588 --> 01:41:13.953
They've got too much evidence.


01:41:13.990 --> 01:41:14.957
(sobbing)


01:41:14.991 --> 01:41:17.016
Come on. I can't.


01:41:17.060 --> 01:41:18.220
Please, please, please,
I'm begging you.


01:41:18.261 --> 01:41:19.228
I can't.


01:41:19.262 --> 01:41:22.231
- I beg you. I beg you.
- Amira, please.


01:41:22.332 --> 01:41:24.232
I beg you!
I beg you!


01:41:24.300 --> 01:41:26.199
Please, please help.


01:41:26.234 --> 01:41:28.031
I can't. I can't.


01:41:29.771 --> 01:41:31.033
(cries)


01:42:00.433 --> 01:42:02.924
##


01:42:34.297 --> 01:42:37.528
I was determined
not to blame you.


01:42:37.567 --> 01:42:40.365
And I know it wasn't your fault,
I know it wasn't this afternoon.


01:42:40.404 --> 01:42:44.203
I'm sorry, I'm
sorry, I'm sorry.


01:42:44.240 --> 01:42:47.607
No, it's me
who should be saying sorry.


01:42:54.717 --> 01:42:58.812
I've been looking for love...


01:42:58.853 --> 01:43:00.844
out there.


01:43:03.258 --> 01:43:06.250
I thought I might have found it.


01:43:10.130 --> 01:43:11.495
And did you?


01:43:13.167 --> 01:43:15.601
I think I might have lost
the love I did have.


01:43:18.105 --> 01:43:21.006
The love of my life.


01:43:25.378 --> 01:43:27.869
Did I?


01:43:33.953 --> 01:43:35.852
Liv, I need to tell you
everything.


01:43:35.887 --> 01:43:38.412
I need to tell you
what I've done.


01:43:54.138 --> 01:43:57.596
##


01:44:19.394 --> 01:44:21.419
I thought you were going.


01:44:21.463 --> 01:44:25.627
I can't go.


01:44:25.667 --> 01:44:28.499
I slept with her.


01:44:28.536 --> 01:44:31.300
It was hard enough
to tell you that last night.


01:44:31.339 --> 01:44:34.206
That was bad enough
without saying it in public,


01:44:34.242 --> 01:44:37.541
without hurting you twice.


01:44:41.915 --> 01:44:44.509
When you hurt this much,
you can't be hurt twice.


01:44:47.387 --> 01:44:51.221
I was looking at you...


01:44:51.258 --> 01:44:54.818
and I was thinking how long
since I'd looked at you.


01:44:57.029 --> 01:45:00.692
I don't even know how
to be honest.


01:45:00.733 --> 01:45:03.167
Maybe that's why
I like metaphors.


01:45:03.269 --> 01:45:08.262
Because what I want to say
is there's a circle--


01:45:08.306 --> 01:45:11.366
yours and Bea's--
and I'm not in it.


01:45:15.446 --> 01:45:19.905
But that's just to justify it,
because there's a part of me


01:45:19.950 --> 01:45:24.546
so dark,
that sees that circle as a cage.


01:45:39.168 --> 01:45:40.362
Thanks.


01:45:40.403 --> 01:45:42.337
Will.


01:45:42.371 --> 01:45:43.598
You made it.


01:45:51.279 --> 01:45:54.214
(indistinct chatter)


01:45:54.249 --> 01:45:57.411
WOMAN:
Come in and sit down.


01:45:58.452 --> 01:46:00.215
I'm sorry, there, um...


01:46:00.287 --> 01:46:02.255
th-this is, there's
been a big mistake.


01:46:02.289 --> 01:46:03.950
- Mistake?
- Yeah, um...


01:46:03.991 --> 01:46:06.551
Yeah. This boy is definitely
not the burglar.


01:46:06.594 --> 01:46:09.391
I know him, and I know
his... I know his mother.


01:46:09.429 --> 01:46:11.454
MAN: What do you mean
you know them?


01:46:11.497 --> 01:46:14.091
They came to our office.
They came to the office.


01:46:14.133 --> 01:46:15.259
Well, how can that be?


01:46:15.301 --> 01:46:16.359
You were told their names,


01:46:16.402 --> 01:46:17.528
yet you never said
you recognized them.


01:46:17.570 --> 01:46:19.936
I don't remember you
saying the name "Simic."


01:46:19.973 --> 01:46:21.497
You definitely
didn't say "Simic."


01:46:21.541 --> 01:46:22.632
Miro and I know each other.


01:46:22.674 --> 01:46:25.108
Actually, very well.


01:46:25.143 --> 01:46:26.167
Um, Miro is,


01:46:26.244 --> 01:46:28.439
um, interested in architecture.


01:46:28.480 --> 01:46:30.175
Mrs. Simic?


01:46:30.282 --> 01:46:31.544
He is, yes.


01:46:31.583 --> 01:46:33.813
No, I'm asking is it true
that you and Mr...


01:46:33.852 --> 01:46:35.716
Um, Francis.


01:46:35.753 --> 01:46:37.243
Francis-- know each other?


01:46:40.291 --> 01:46:44.387
Mr. Francis is, um,
I've done some work for him,


01:46:44.428 --> 01:46:45.918
adjusting his suit.


01:46:45.963 --> 01:46:48.556
I think this Mrs.-- Mrs., um,


01:46:48.598 --> 01:46:53.558
Amira is being... discreet.


01:46:53.603 --> 01:46:56.333
What do you mean, discreet?


01:46:58.375 --> 01:47:04.244
Amira is being discreet about
the nature of our relationship,


01:47:04.279 --> 01:47:07.510
which was not
an appropriate one,


01:47:07.549 --> 01:47:10.575
and I think she's trying to
save me from embarrassment,


01:47:10.619 --> 01:47:14.452
from the embarrassment
of myself and my family.


01:47:14.489 --> 01:47:18.926
And that's why she, um,
that's why she's not saying


01:47:18.960 --> 01:47:21.155
sh-she came to the office
with Miro.


01:47:21.229 --> 01:47:23.993
I remember it, though; it was
the day of the last burglary.


01:47:24.032 --> 01:47:25.431
(clears throat)


01:47:25.466 --> 01:47:26.524
And Miro cut his hand,


01:47:26.567 --> 01:47:28.659
and that's obviously
where the, uh,


01:47:28.702 --> 01:47:31.933
well, that's where the
DNA confusion occurred.


01:47:34.574 --> 01:47:36.303
Mr. Hoffman?


01:47:36.343 --> 01:47:38.311
Mr. Hoffman, do you know
anything about this?


01:47:38.345 --> 01:47:41.336
No. No, I can't say I do.


01:47:41.380 --> 01:47:42.540
Is this some sort of--


01:47:42.581 --> 01:47:44.708
I mean, are we supposed
to believe this?


01:47:44.750 --> 01:47:48.186
Actually, I've met
both of them at the office.


01:47:48.254 --> 01:47:50.950
Yes.


01:47:50.990 --> 01:47:54.982
And I-I dressed
the boy's cut, didn't I?


01:47:55.026 --> 01:47:57.460
WILL (softly):
Yeah.


01:47:57.495 --> 01:47:59.827
MAN:
Wai-- hang on a minute.


01:47:59.864 --> 01:48:01.957
We recalled a computer,
which you claimed


01:48:02.000 --> 01:48:04.195
had been stolen.


01:48:05.370 --> 01:48:06.700
Yeah, I lent


01:48:06.737 --> 01:48:08.796
(clears throat):
I lent Mrs. Simic my laptop


01:48:08.839 --> 01:48:11.706
sometime when we
were, um, together.


01:48:11.742 --> 01:48:13.972
She takes photographs,


01:48:14.011 --> 01:48:15.945
and I was showing her
how to store them,


01:48:15.979 --> 01:48:20.176
um, what to do with them,
how to delete them.


01:48:21.851 --> 01:48:24.911
I'd completely
forgotten; I was, um...


01:48:24.954 --> 01:48:27.149
(sighs)


01:48:27.190 --> 01:48:28.714
I was confused.


01:48:32.594 --> 01:48:34.926
I'm sorry.


01:48:38.066 --> 01:48:39.931
Really sorry.


01:48:56.650 --> 01:49:00.346
##


01:49:17.236 --> 01:49:20.171
##


01:49:51.967 --> 01:49:54.663
What you did back there,


01:49:54.703 --> 01:49:58.469
you gave that boy back
his life.


01:50:06.281 --> 01:50:09.045
Stop the car.


01:50:09.083 --> 01:50:10.345
What?


01:50:10.385 --> 01:50:11.374
Liv, what are you doing?


01:50:11.419 --> 01:50:13.649
You just don't get it,
do you?


01:50:13.688 --> 01:50:14.847
- What?
- Oh, God.


01:50:14.888 --> 01:50:16.617
We just go home, right?


01:50:16.657 --> 01:50:18.352
We just go home, nothing
happened, nothing happened.


01:50:18.392 --> 01:50:19.654
- (horn honking)
- Liv?


01:50:19.693 --> 01:50:21.786
- Go, go to Bosnia, go!
- I can't hear you.


01:50:21.829 --> 01:50:23.820
Get back in the car, Liv.


01:50:23.864 --> 01:50:25.525
Just go, go.


01:50:25.566 --> 01:50:26.965
(horn honking)


01:50:27.000 --> 01:50:28.694
Why were you looking for love?


01:50:28.734 --> 01:50:30.634
Ask yourself. Why?


01:50:30.670 --> 01:50:33.366
Why weren't you looking for me?


01:50:33.406 --> 01:50:34.668
Liv, get back in the car.


01:50:34.707 --> 01:50:37.938
No. I don't want you
in the house!


01:50:37.977 --> 01:50:39.706
I don't want you in the house!


01:50:39.745 --> 01:50:41.439
God!


01:50:41.479 --> 01:50:43.777
God, you drive me out.


01:50:43.815 --> 01:50:45.146
You marry me then!


01:50:45.183 --> 01:50:46.514
No, I don't want a husband!


01:50:46.551 --> 01:50:47.711
I want a good night's sleep.


01:50:47.752 --> 01:50:49.219
No. Marry me.


01:50:49.287 --> 01:50:50.345
- No.
- Marry me.


01:50:50.388 --> 01:50:51.480
- I'm sorry.
- No!


01:50:51.523 --> 01:50:52.615
I want you back.


01:50:52.657 --> 01:50:54.214
- Then win me back.
- How?


01:50:54.291 --> 01:50:55.315
I don't know.


01:50:55.359 --> 01:50:56.553
How? What will I do?
What do I do?


01:50:56.594 --> 01:50:59.461
- I don't know!
- I've been such an idiot.


01:50:59.496 --> 01:51:00.986
Just tell me what I have to do.


01:51:01.031 --> 01:51:02.896
I don't know!


01:51:02.933 --> 01:51:04.867
Look, I love you.


01:51:04.902 --> 01:51:06.493
I love you.


01:51:09.072 --> 01:51:11.097
Oh, God, I'm so sorry.


01:51:11.140 --> 01:51:12.937
I'm so sorry.


01:51:38.199 --> 01:51:39.826
Mirsad.


01:51:40.868 --> 01:51:42.426
We never met, did we;
I'm Will.


01:51:42.470 --> 01:51:43.960
Hi.


01:51:44.005 --> 01:51:45.494
So you're off to Sarajevo?


01:51:45.538 --> 01:51:47.130
You wanted to say something,
right?


01:51:47.173 --> 01:51:49.368
I just wanted to say
that I'm sorry.


01:51:49.409 --> 01:51:50.535
- And...
- Wait.


01:51:50.577 --> 01:51:53.671
Sandy, have you got
a minute?


01:52:02.721 --> 01:52:04.951
I just wanted to say
that I was sorry


01:52:04.990 --> 01:52:06.719
and thanks for what you did.


01:52:06.759 --> 01:52:09.751
You've given me another chance.


01:52:10.763 --> 01:52:13.026
Okay, thanks for coming in.


01:52:13.064 --> 01:52:15.362
Thank you.


01:52:15.400 --> 01:52:19.860
This, I think, is the stuff
my mom mended for you.


01:52:22.307 --> 01:52:24.900
Tell her...


01:52:24.942 --> 01:52:28.605
tell her thanks
for mending stuff for me.


01:52:32.649 --> 01:52:37.642
WILL: I thought maybe your
mother would come with you.


01:52:37.687 --> 01:52:40.656
Yeah, she was going to,
but she's packing.


01:52:40.690 --> 01:52:43.386
Is she?


01:52:43.426 --> 01:52:46.054
Thank you.


01:53:14.121 --> 01:53:17.715
(chatting softly)


01:53:21.127 --> 01:53:25.325
(chatting indistinctly)


01:53:25.365 --> 01:53:26.662
What is this?


01:53:56.693 --> 01:54:00.493
##


01:54:31.959 --> 01:54:35.189
(woman singing high-pitched
soft notes in foreign language)


01:54:44.004 --> 01:54:48.099
(chorus joins in)


01:55:17.634 --> 01:55:21.092
##


01:55:51.065 --> 01:55:54.057
##


01:56:23.262 --> 01:56:26.959
##


01:56:56.825 --> 01:57:00.886
##


01:57:30.657 --> 01:57:34.649
##


01:58:04.321 --> 01:58:07.916
##


01:58:31.647 --> 01:58:35.105
##

